      "type": "network_diagram",
      "title": "How DNS resolves a domain",
      "durationInSeconds": 21.75,
      "narration": "Your browser doesn't know where to find that website \u2014 so it asks a DNS resolver. The resolver checks its cache first. If it's a miss, it asks the root server. The root server points to the TLD server. The TLD server points to the authoritative server. The authoritative server finally returns the IP address \u2014 four round trips, all under 20 milliseconds.",
